# tron plugin — environment variables
#
# The Confluence / content skills read these from the shell environment.
# On the reference setup they live in ~/.env (generated by 1Password) and are
# auto-sourced; the bundled fetch-confluence.sh also sources ~/.env on demand if a
# token is missing. Copy the keys you need into your own ~/.env (or export them in
# your shell, or add them to your marketing-pages .env.local), then fill in real
# values. NEVER commit real secrets — this file is the template, not the secret store.
#
# Tools that authenticate on their own (acli, gh, codex) are NOT listed here — log
# into those separately (`acli jira auth`, `gh auth login`, `codex login`).

# --- Atlassian (Jira + Confluence) ---

# As of MD-1995, fetch-confluence.sh's page-body fetch and attachment *listing*
# try the org-secret broker first (secrets.facilitron.work — same pattern as
# ImageKit/Figma/CircleCI below), so these two vars are no longer needed for
# that path. They're still used as a fallback (broker unreachable) and for the
# attachment *download* leg, which hits api.atlassian.com — a host the broker
# doesn't proxy yet (blocked on MD-2011). See tools/jira/broker-status.md.

# Your Atlassian account email. Used for the Confluence direct-auth fallback and
# the image-attachment download path (tron:news-item, tron:guide-item). If unset,
# the fetch script falls back to `git config user.email`.
ATLASSIAN_EMAIL=you@facilitron.com

# Atlassian API token — create at:
#   https://id.atlassian.com/manage-profile/security/api-tokens
# Used by tron:confluence, tron:news-item, tron:guide-item for the direct-auth
# fallback and attachment downloads.
JIRA_API_TOKEN=

# Optional — override the Confluence target. Defaults point at Facilitron's instance,
# so leave these unset unless you're pointing the content skills at a different site.
# CONFLUENCE_CLOUD_ID=91c1b48f-c272-40fb-9c7f-cc5f23bb74d7
# CONFLUENCE_BASE=https://facilitron.atlassian.net/wiki

# --- ImageKit / Figma / CircleCI ---
#
# These are org-shared credentials, brokered through the org-secret broker at
# secrets.facilitron.work — the ImageKit CLI, the Figma REST fallback in
# tron:figma-to-imagekit, and tron:circleci all authenticate with a short-lived
# Cloudflare Access token (`cloudflared access login https://secrets.facilitron.work`)
# instead of a local key. No IMAGEKIT_PRIVATE_KEY / FIGMA_ACCESS_TOKEN / CIRCLECI_TOKEN
# needed here.
